        "chunk_order": 15,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "programme",
      "subcategory": "curriculum",
      "field": "content",
      "value": "Various market structures exist. In perfectly competitive markets, no participant is large enough to have the market power to set the price of a homogeneous product. In other words, every participant is a 'price taker' because no single participant can influence the product's price. In the real world, markets often experience imperfect competition.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source_url": "",
      "source_type": "",
      "programme_association": "",
